  "note": "Annual election of three commissioners; poll Monday 16 May 1938 (15 May was a Sunday). Five nominations were received, two were withdrawn, and the remaining three were returned unopposed. Poll day Monday 16 May 1938 (15 May was a Sunday); returned unopposed. (round folder corrected from \"1938-05 approx\", 5 Nov 2026) William M'Kinney and Cecil Ormsby Wylie withdrew their nominations, leaving three candidates for three seats. Returned unopposed."
